1
00:00:03,560 --> 00:00:05,430
你有没有听说过这个研究  它的结果显示
Did you hear about this study that found people

2
00:00:05,430 --> 00:00:07,750
在13岁左右很酷  很受欢迎的人
that were cool and popular at 13

3
00:00:07,750 --> 00:00:09,570
在之后的人生中  通常较难获得成功
have problems succeeding later in life?

4
00:00:09,570 --> 00:00:12,250
我现在就还行啊  我13岁时也很受欢迎
I'm doing okay, and I was very popular at 13.

5
00:00:12,250 --> 00:00:13,100
在学校吗
In school?

6
00:00:13,100 --> 00:00:14,710
不是  在家
Oh, no. At home.

7
00:00:15,440 --> 00:00:16,990
佣人们会给我唱歌
The servants would sing to me,

8
00:00:16,990 --> 00:00:19,070
会捧场我的笑话
laugh at my jokes...

9
00:00:20,410 --> 00:00:23,180
真希望我知道他们的名字
I wish I knew their names.

10
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:26,220
研究有说不受欢迎的孩子之后会如何吗
Does the study say what happens to the unpopular kids?

11
00:00:26,220 --> 00:00:28,870
你说呢  你每天起床时身旁就有一个
You tell me-- you woke up in bed with one.

12
00:00:30,570 --> 00:00:31,720
你们听我说
Listen to this.

13
00:00:31,720 --> 00:00:34,350
我刚收到威尔·惠顿的电邮
I just received an e-mail from Wil Wheaton.

14
00:00:34,350 --> 00:00:37,450
伦纳德·尼莫伊的儿子在拍一部纪录片
Leonard Nimoy's son is working on a documentary

15
00:00:37,450 --> 00:00:39,710
在他爸爸过世前就开始拍摄了
that he started with his father before he passed away.

16
00:00:39,710 --> 00:00:42,610
主题是史波克先生及他对我们文化的影响
It's about Mr. Spock and his impact on our culture.

17
00:00:39,710 --> 00:00:44,130
演员伦纳德·尼莫伊最著名的角色
是《星际旅行》中的史波克

18
00:00:42,610 --> 00:00:44,130
那他为啥要写信给你
Why is he writing to you?

19
00:00:44,130 --> 00:00:46,170
他们想找尼莫伊先生的粉丝做访问
Well, they're looking for fans to interview,

20
00:00:46,170 --> 00:00:47,670
威尔觉得我挺适合
and Wil thought I'd be good for it.

21
00:00:47,670 --> 00:00:48,770
击个掌
Oh. Hey, high five.

22
00:00:48,940 --> 00:00:50,630
打死都不要
Absolutely not.

23
00:00:51,670 --> 00:00:53,000
佩妮
Yeah, Penny,

24
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:54,680
你曾有过出镜的经验
you spent some time in front of the camera.

25
00:00:54,680 --> 00:00:56,220
有何建议吗
Any words of advice?

26
00:00:56,220 --> 00:00:57,540
有  别因为导演叫你脱
Yes. Don't take your shirt off

27
00:00:57,540 --> 00:00:59,800
你就真的脱光
just because the director said so.

28
00:01:00,550 --> 00:01:02,510
这是关于史巴克先生的纪录片
This is a documentary about Mr. Spock.

29
00:01:02,510 --> 00:01:06,020
就算真有裸露镜头  也一定很有品味
I'm sure if there's nudity, it will be tasteful.

30
00:01:24,900 --> 00:01:26,400
生

31
00:01:24,900 --> 00:01:26,400
活

32
00:01:24,900 --> 00:01:26,400
大

33
00:01:24,900 --> 00:01:26,400
爆

34
00:01:24,900 --> 00:01:26,400
炸

35
00:01:24,900 --> 00:01:26,400
第九季  第七集

36
00:01:37,360 --> 00:01:39,060
有空吗
Hey. You got a minute?

37
00:01:39,340 --> 00:01:40,430
不太有
Not really.

38
00:01:40,430 --> 00:01:43,430
我跟西哥特人正战得难分难解呢
Visigoths are kind of up my butt right now.

39
00:01:44,130 --> 00:01:46,080
暂停游戏  霍华德
Pause the game, Howard.

40
00:01:46,080 --> 00:01:47,450
叫"霍华德"  惨了
"Howard"? Uh-oh.

41
00:01:47,450 --> 00:01:49,440
先别碍事  西哥特人
Make room, Visigoths.

42
00:01:50,880 --> 00:01:51,810
怎么了
'Sup?

43
00:01:52,170 --> 00:01:54,270
我们得来谈谈重新装修这房子的事
We need to talk about redecorating this place.

44
00:01:54,270 --> 00:01:56,480
不是吧  又来
Oh, no, not this again.

45
00:01:56,820 --> 00:01:59,000
我理解你从小在这里长大
Look, I get that you grew up here

46
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:01,980
你对屋里的一切有着特殊的感情  可...
and you're attached to things looking a certain way, but...

47
00:02:01,980 --> 00:02:04,140
我也想把这里当自己家
I want this to feel like my house, too.

48
00:02:04,140 --> 00:02:07,070
亲爱的  这里当然是你自己家啦
Oh, honey, of course it's your house.

49
00:02:07,070 --> 00:02:10,280
不然你整天打扫它干嘛
Why else would you be cleaning it all the time?

50
00:02:12,130 --> 00:02:14,020
好吧  我换个方式说
All right. Let's start over.

51
00:02:14,020 --> 00:02:15,560
老娘要装修
I'm redecorating.

52
00:02:15,560 --> 00:02:17,530
家具  地毯  墙都要重弄
The furniture, the carpeting, the walls.

53
00:02:17,530 --> 00:02:20,580
老娘要把看了会郁闷的东西全换掉
I'm changing everything that depresses me when I look at it.

54
00:02:20,580 --> 00:02:22,880
试着别让自己也变其中一员
Try not to be one of those things.

55
00:02:23,800 --> 00:02:25,260
我能说一件事吗
May I say something?

56
00:02:25,260 --> 00:02:27,130
是想说我不能换掉墙纸
Is it about how I can't have new wallpaper

57
00:02:27,130 --> 00:02:29,770
因为你爹打小就离开你  你娘还过世了吗
'cause your dad left when you were little and your mom died?

58
00:02:29,770 --> 00:02:31,510
没事儿了
Never mind.

59
00:02:34,590 --> 00:02:36,340
艾米  是我谢尔顿
Hello, Amy. It's Sheldon.

60
00:02:36,340 --> 00:02:38,120
我知道我们已经分手了
Yeah, I-I know that we're broken up,

61
00:02:38,120 --> 00:02:39,530
但我给你留言
but I'm leaving this message

62
00:02:39,530 --> 00:02:41,590
是觉得你可能有兴趣看我
because I thought perhaps you'd like to watch me

63
00:02:41,590 --> 00:02:44,590
在史波克先生的纪录片中接受访问
be interviewed for a documentary about Mr. Spock.

64
00:02:44,590 --> 00:02:48,200
或者我更爱称之为是"史"记
Or as I like to call it, a Spockumentary.

65
00:02:48,890 --> 00:02:51,160
我会在纪录片里讲这个哏
Yeah, I'm going to use that joke in the interview,

66
00:02:51,160 --> 00:02:53,900
你看时尽量像第一次听到那样笑出来哦
so try to laugh like you're hearing it for the first time.

67
00:02:53,900 --> 00:02:56,150
你懂吧  笑到抽筋
You know, hysterically, hmm?

68
00:02:56,150 --> 00:02:59,210
但是又带有一点我已不在身边的悲伤
And with a tinge of sadness that I'm no longer in your life.

69
00:03:00,100 --> 00:03:02,280
我才是想出"史"记这名字的人
I'm the one who thought of "Spockumentary""

70
00:03:02,280 --> 00:03:05,440
而我正像第一次听到那样笑着呢
And I'm laughing like I did the first time I heard it.

71
00:03:09,030 --> 00:03:09,960
你们好
Hello.

72
00:03:09,960 --> 00:03:10,870
你好  谢尔顿
Hey, Sheldon.

73
00:03:10,870 --> 00:03:11,860
这位是亚当·尼莫伊
This is Adam Nimoy.

74
00:03:11,860 --> 00:03:14,540
-幸会  -我也很高兴见到你
- Nice to meet you. - Oh, it's nice to meet you.

75
00:03:14,540 --> 00:03:16,880
我十分钦佩您父亲的作品
I admire your father's work very much.

76
00:03:16,880 --> 00:03:19,150
而能见到从自己偶像的阴囊中
It's not every day I get to meet someone whose life's journey

77
00:03:19,150 --> 00:03:21,910
开始人生旅途的人  也很稀奇
began in my hero's scrotum.

78
00:03:24,800 --> 00:03:27,550
我就跟你说这家伙绝对极品
I told you. This guy is gold.

79
00:03:31,990 --> 00:03:32,880
你在干嘛
Whatcha doing? Oh!

80
00:03:33,220 --> 00:03:36,040
给自己做我爹离家后  我妈去世前
Making myself a bologna sandwich like my mom used to make me

81
00:03:36,040 --> 00:03:39,140
她会给我做的腊肠三明治
after my dad left, but before she died.

82
00:03:42,900 --> 00:03:44,350
好啦  我在想
Okay, listen, I'm thinking

83
00:03:44,350 --> 00:03:47,360
或许房子这件事我们可以有个折衷办法
that maybe we can compromise on the house.

84
00:03:47,590 --> 00:03:49,050
我听着呢
I'm listening.

85
00:03:49,050 --> 00:03:52,220
我们可以先装修一个房间  看看效果如何
Let's just redo one room and see how it goes.

86
00:03:52,220 --> 00:03:53,740
此言有理
That is reasonable.

87
00:03:53,740 --> 00:03:55,630
但装修哪间房间呢
But what room?

88
00:03:55,630 --> 00:03:57,890
-比如这间  -绝对不行
- How 'bout this one? - No way.

89
00:03:57,890 --> 00:04:01,640
不行  这是我跟我妈互动最多的房间
No way, this is the room I associate the most with my mom.

90
00:04:01,640 --> 00:04:03,410
那浴室呢
Then how about the bathroom?

91
00:04:03,410 --> 00:04:06,030
其实我们互动最多是在浴室
I want to change my answer.

92
00:04:07,390 --> 00:04:09,460
好吧  那饭厅呢
Fine. Then the dining room.

93
00:04:09,900 --> 00:04:11,920
我们的确是比较不常用那里
I guess we didn't use it very often.

94
00:04:11,920 --> 00:04:13,040
只有有伴时才用
Unless we had company.

95
00:04:13,040 --> 00:04:15,550
不过在我爹离家后  那就不怎么用了
Which didn't happen much after my dad left and not at all

96
00:04:15,550 --> 00:04:17,680
-我妈去世后更是...  -很好  我去挑油漆样本
- after my mom... - Great! I'm gonna go pick out paint samples.

97
00:04:21,490 --> 00:04:23,040
好的  我们就自然对话
All right, we're just gonna have a conversation.

98
00:04:23,040 --> 00:04:25,320
假装没有镜头在拍你就行了
Pretend the camera's not here.

99
00:04:25,320 --> 00:04:28,380
好  但这最好不是精心设计来
All right. But this better not be some elaborate scheme

100
00:04:28,380 --> 00:04:30,220
要骗人家宽衣解带的骗局
to get me out of my shirt.

101
00:04:32,080 --> 00:04:33,590
你跟亚当认识多久了
How long have you known Adam?

102
00:04:33,590 --> 00:04:34,670
几年了
A few years.

103
00:04:35,030 --> 00:04:37,850
他是哪里得罪你了
And what are you getting him back for?

104
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:41,170
先从你的名字与职业说起吧
Let's start with your name and occupation.

105
00:04:41,170 --> 00:04:45,240
谢尔顿·库伯博士  加州理工理论物理学家
Dr. Sheldon Cooper, theoretical physicist, Caltech.

106
00:04:45,240 --> 00:04:49,400
你对史波克这角色最早的记忆是什么呢
And what is your earliest memory of the character Spock?

107
00:04:49,400 --> 00:04:53,450
《星际旅行:原初》系列中  我第一次看
The first episode of StarTrek: The Original Series I ever saw

108
00:04:53,450 --> 00:04:55,350
是第1季第16集
was "The Galileo Seven."

109
00:04:55,350 --> 00:04:58,770
史巴克在金牛座2号星上降落
Uh, Spock had just landed on the planet Taurus II.

110
00:04:58,770 --> 00:05:01,230
然后我哥走进来  坐在我头上
Then my brother came in, sat on my head,

111
00:05:01,230 --> 00:05:03,340
然后说"吃屁吧"
and said, "Eat farts."

112
00:05:04,780 --> 00:05:06,730
那次之后  我就着迷了
After that day, I was hooked.

113
00:05:06,730 --> 00:05:08,250
对《星际旅行》着迷
On Star Trek,

114
00:05:08,250 --> 00:05:11,930
不是对我哥的"菊花餐点"着迷
not my brother's sphincter-based cuisine.

115
00:05:13,150 --> 00:05:16,170
史波克是哪一点吸引到了你呢
What was it about Spock that appealed to you?

116
00:05:16,170 --> 00:05:19,170
我想所有被吸引的人  都是因为同个理由吧
I think the same thing that appeals to people everywhere,

117
00:05:19,170 --> 00:05:22,030
梦想着一个冷酷理智的世界
the dream of a cold, rational world

118
00:05:22,030 --> 00:05:24,570
完全没有任何人类情感
entirely without human emotion.

119
00:05:25,140 --> 00:05:28,090
史波克来自只讲逻辑的地方
Spock came from a planet governed only by logic.

120
00:05:28,090 --> 00:05:30,320
在他家乡瓦肯星上  如果你的哥哥问你
You know, on Vulcan, when your brother asks,

121
00:05:30,320 --> 00:05:31,690
"你为什么要打自己"
"Why are you hitting yourself?"

122
00:05:31,690 --> 00:05:34,300
那答案会是  "我没有啊
The answer is, "I'm not.

123
00:05:34,300 --> 00:05:36,560
是你在控制我的手"
You're moving my arm."

124
00:05:37,470 --> 00:05:39,800
然后他会回答"太有意思了"
To which he says, "Fascinating."

125
00:05:39,800 --> 00:05:43,020
于是你们就一起看教育频道
And then you both watch educational television.

126
00:05:43,910 --> 00:05:45,450
听到他说这类事情时
Aw. When he says things like that,

127
00:05:45,450 --> 00:05:48,010
我就想过去抱抱他  哄哄他
I just want to hug him and make everything better.

128
00:05:48,010 --> 00:05:49,840
我哥对我也很坏啊
My brother was mean to me, too.

129
00:05:49,840 --> 00:05:52,070
你绝对是自己找揍
Yeah, you probably had it coming.

130
00:05:53,230 --> 00:05:55,290
你有任何史波克的收藏品吗
Do you have any Spock collectibles?

131
00:05:55,290 --> 00:05:56,570
我有很多啊
I have many.

132
00:05:56,570 --> 00:05:59,060
但最珍贵的是尼莫伊先生亲笔签名的餐巾
My most treasured is an autographed napkin

133
00:05:59,060 --> 00:06:01,750
来自我体贴的好友佩妮
given to me by my very thoughtful friend Penny.

134
00:05:59,060 --> 00:06:03,310
在第2季第11集时送的
尼莫伊先生在2015年2月已去世

135
00:06:01,750 --> 00:06:03,310
她就在那边
That's her over there.

136
00:06:06,020 --> 00:06:07,000
大家好
Hi!

137
00:06:08,910 --> 00:06:09,490
瞧瞧
Look at that.

138
00:06:09,490 --> 00:06:11,540
不用脱衣服就能出镜了呢
I'm in a movie, my shirt stayed on.

139
00:06:13,340 --> 00:06:14,930
我们能看看那块餐巾吗
Can we see the napkin?

140
00:06:14,930 --> 00:06:16,510
当然  失陪一下
Of course. Excuse me.

141
00:06:16,510 --> 00:06:18,370
拿出来得费点功夫
This will just take a moment.

142
00:06:29,910 --> 00:06:32,300
墙式保险箱什么时候装的
When did we get a wall safe?

143
00:06:33,820 --> 00:06:36,550
在地板保险箱装满之后啊
When there was no more room in the floor safe.

144
00:06:36,990 --> 00:06:39,750
地板保险箱又什么时候装的
When did we get a floor safe?

145
00:06:39,750 --> 00:06:42,130
装了监控摄像机之后啊
When we got the security camera.

146
00:06:42,130 --> 00:06:44,490
还有监控摄像机吗
There's a security camera?

147
00:06:45,350 --> 00:06:48,880
潜水侠  自2012年以来一直保护你家
Aquaman, protecting your home since 2012.

148
00:06:50,940 --> 00:06:53,150
老天  我们在沙发上"做"过好些事情
Oh, my God. We've done things on that couch.

149
00:06:53,150 --> 00:06:55,200
是啊  你不说我也知道
Yeah. You don't have to tell me.

150
00:06:58,250 --> 00:07:00,260
你的岳父现在在这呢
So, your father-in-law is in there right now?

151
00:07:00,260 --> 00:07:01,480
是的  你要帮我说话
Yes. So back me up.

152
00:07:01,480 --> 00:07:03,770
-就说这房子维持原样就好  -好的  哦了
- The house is good the way it is. - Oh, okay. Got it.

153
00:07:05,150 --> 00:07:06,770
在忙什么呢
Hey. What's going on?

154
00:07:06,770 --> 00:07:08,180
你好  拉杰
Hey. Hey, Raj.

155
00:07:08,180 --> 00:07:10,680
我和爸爸在讨论把这面墙拆掉
Dad and I were just talking about taking down this wall.

156
00:07:10,680 --> 00:07:14,190
你确定吗  这可是...一面好墙啊
You sure? It's a... pretty great wall.

157
00:07:15,610 --> 00:07:17,330
好在哪里
What's so great about it?

158
00:07:18,070 --> 00:07:20,120
很抱歉  我尽力了
I'm sorry. I did what I could.

159
00:07:21,880 --> 00:07:24,200
不是吧  你把拉杰带过来帮你站队吗
Seriously? You brought Raj over to take your side?

160
00:07:24,200 --> 00:07:25,760
你爸跟你是一队
Your dad's on your side.

161
00:07:25,760 --> 00:07:28,920
他才没有站队  他是过来免费帮忙的
He's not on my side. He's doing all the work for free.

162
00:07:28,920 --> 00:07:31,730
你真是太慷慨无私了
That is so generous of you.

163
00:07:32,380 --> 00:07:34,540
我想换一队站
I'd like to switch sides.

164
00:07:35,890 --> 00:07:36,450
听着
Look, uh...

165
00:07:36,770 --> 00:07:38,280
我觉得你们不能把这面墙拆掉
I don't even think you can take this wall down

166
00:07:38,280 --> 00:07:39,500
因为它是承重墙
'cause it's load-bearing.

167
00:07:39,500 --> 00:07:40,520
想知道很容易
Well, it's easy to find out.

168
00:07:40,520 --> 00:07:43,420
只要爬到房子和地基中间的夹层  一试便知
Just go into the crawlspace under the house and check.

169
00:07:43,420 --> 00:07:46,140
你的签证什么时候到期
When is your visa up?

170
00:07:48,800 --> 00:07:50,820
这上面不仅有署名给我的签名
Not only is it signed to me

171
00:07:50,820 --> 00:07:53,120
而且这里  还是他擦过嘴的地方
but this is where he wiped his mouth.

172
00:07:53,120 --> 00:07:57,430
现在在大家面前的是伦纳德·尼莫伊的DNA
So we are currently in the presence of Leonard Nimoy's DNA.

173
00:07:57,430 --> 00:08:01,170
亚当不算是伦纳德·尼莫伊的DNA吗
Um, doesn't Adam count as Leonard Nimoy's DNA?

174
00:08:01,800 --> 00:08:05,060
无意冒犯  但这可是100%纯尼莫伊
No offense, but this is pure 100% Nimoy.

175
00:08:05,060 --> 00:08:08,510
而因为你妈  你只有50%的种
Because of your mother, you're only 50%.

176
00:08:09,050 --> 00:08:10,250
这也不是坏事
